---
import ArrowIcon from './ArrowIcon.astro';
import PatternCarousel from './PatternCarousel.astro';
import { behavioralPatternsUrl } from '../data/site';
---

<section class="skills" id="keyskills" aria-labelledby="keyskills-title" data-nav-section="keyskills">
  <div class="container skills__intro">
    <h2 class="t-display reveal" id="keyskills-title">Key Skills</h2>
    <p class="t-lead skills__lead reveal">
      Besides making everything pretty, a11y, readable, understandable, easily digestible, and
      minimizing cognitive load, I developed a set of key skills that are crucial to deliver great
      results.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="container skills__block skills__block--patterns">
    <h3 class="t-heading reveal">Ergonomy &amp; Psychology</h3>
    <div class="skills__text reveal">
      <p>
        Every single interaction anywhere, anytime requires an initial impulse, motivation, and
        effort to complete. The higher the motivation, the more effort users will accept to achieve
        their goals. To maximize user interaction, Experience Designers combine two powerful tools:
      </p>
      <p>
        Behavioral patterns, which leverage a wide variety of psychological triggers (see below)
        that persuade users to take action and
      </p>
      <p>
        UI patterns, which implement those behavioral patterns in the form of best practice
        components that help the users to complete their tasks and achieve their goals.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <PatternCarousel />

  <div class="container skills__block skills__block--after-carousel">
    <p class="reveal">
      In the last two decades, I’ve worked with more and more of those roundabout 120 patterns
      consciously and have lots of experience choosing and implementing the right ones and thereby
      boosting business significantly.
    </p>
    <a class="button reveal" href={behavioralPatternsUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      All Behavioral Patterns <ArrowIcon tight />
    </a>
  </div>

  <article class="container skills__block">
    <h3 class="t-heading reveal">Business &amp; Constraints</h3>
    <div class="skills__text reveal">
      <p>
        To provide effective consulting, it’s essential to understand a company and its ecosystem as
        a whole. This includes analyzing the business model, industry landscape, competitors,
        trends, and target audience, as well as considering all existing products, services, and
        technical, legal and economical constraints.
      </p>
      <p>
        In over 25 years, I have worked with many large companies from various industries. This has
        not only given me deep knowledge in diverse sectors but also the ability to combine insights
        and learnings across industries and bring new perspectives from the outside.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="button reveal" href="#clients">My Clients <ArrowIcon tight /></a>
  </article>

  <div class="container skills__columns">
    <article class="skills__column">
      <h3 class="t-heading reveal">Designer &amp; Developer</h3>
      <div class="skills__text reveal">
        <p>
          As a UX/UI designer, I combine independent excellence with team leadership capabilities,
          leveraging deep development knowledge to bridge the designer-developer gap.
        </p>
        <p>
          My strategic approach centers on agile prioritization – doing the right things right at
          the right time – while maintaining focus on feasible, iterative implementation for
          business growth.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="skills__column">
      <h3 class="t-heading reveal">Enabler &amp; Facilitator</h3>
      <div class="skills__text reveal">
        <p>
          When not designing, I support teams as a facilitator, using strong communication skills
          to foster open dialogue and constructive conflict resolution. I create a supportive
          environment while maintaining focus and transparency, guiding teams toward their goals.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .skills {
    padding-block: var(--section-space);
  }

  .skills__intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--stack-l);
  }

  .skills__lead {
    max-width: 810px;
  }

  .skills__block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--stack-s);
    padding-top: var(--section-space);
  }

  .skills__block--patterns {
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .skills__block--after-carousel {
    padding-top: var(--stack-l);
  }

  .skills__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .skills__columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--column-gap);
    padding-top: var(--section-space);
  }

  .skills__column {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--stack-s);
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .skills__columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--section-space);
    }
  }
</style>
